TrustMesh modifications include:
- Profile 0.2 site-action approval before every write and irreversible action.
- Read-only-only action bridge exposure for peer networks.
- Two-stage cross-origin consent: public origin discovery approval, followed by a separate exact JSON field disclosure review after network validation.
- Fail-closed behavior when consent UI/callback is unavailable.
- Payload leaf-path and SHA-256 revalidation before peer invocation.
- Deny-by-default private context across peer boundaries.

